  "Google dork: site:target.com cache:": "Steps:\n\n1. Google’s cache can show a page’s content even after it was removed/protected.\n2. View a cached page:\ncache:target.com/path   (or the ‘Cached’ link in results)\n3. Use it to read pages that now require auth or were deleted.\n4. Look for sensitive data that persisted in the cache.\n5. Report data still exposed via cache (recommend cache removal + no-index).\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nSensitive pages remain readable via Google’s cache even after being removed or protected.\n\nSeverity: Low–Medium.",
  "Google dork: site:target.com \"error\" \"sql\"": "Steps:\n\n1. This dork finds indexed pages showing SQL error messages — signs of SQL injection / info leak.\n2. Search:\nsite:target.com \"error\" \"sql\"\n3. Open hits and read the SQL error (reveals queries, tables, DB type).\n4. Revisit the reflecting parameter and test it for SQL injection.\n5. Report verbose SQL errors and any confirmed injection.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nIndexed SQL error pages disclose database internals and often indicate an injectable parameter.\n\nSeverity: Medium (High if injection confirmed).",
  "Google dork: site:pastebin.com target.com": "Steps:\n\n1. This dork searches pastebin.com for references to the target — pasted code/creds/config leaked by employees or attackers.\n2. Search:\nsite:pastebin.com target.com\n3. Open each result and look for leaked data/credentials tied to the target.\n4. Pivot on found usernames/repos/pastes for more leaks.\n5. Report any exposed secrets or sensitive internal information.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThird-party site pastebin.com has indexed content referencing the target that may leak pasted code/creds/config leaked by employees or attackers.\n\nSeverity: Medium",
