  "Test all CRUD operations (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)": "Steps:\n\n1. Take an endpoint and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Try every HTTP method on it: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, OPTIONS (and TRACE).\n3. Look for methods that shouldn’t be allowed but work (e.g. DELETE/PUT without authorization, or write via an unexpected verb).\n4. Check HEAD/OPTIONS for information disclosure (allowed methods, CORS, existence of hidden routes).\n5. Try method override (X-HTTP-Method-Override, _method) to reach restricted verbs.\n6. Confirm improper method handling or a method that bypasses controls.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API mishandles HTTP methods — allowing state-changing verbs without proper authorization, or leaking info via HEAD/OPTIONS/verb override.\n\nSeverity: Medium",
  "Test for improper HTTP method handling on endpoints": "Steps:\n\n1. Take an endpoint and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Try every HTTP method on it: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, OPTIONS (and TRACE).\n3. Look for methods that shouldn’t be allowed but work (e.g. DELETE/PUT without authorization, or write via an unexpected verb).\n4. Check HEAD/OPTIONS for information disclosure (allowed methods, CORS, existence of hidden routes).\n5. Try method override (X-HTTP-Method-Override, _method) to reach restricted verbs.\n6. Confirm improper method handling or a method that bypasses controls.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API mishandles HTTP methods — allowing state-changing verbs without proper authorization, or leaking info via HEAD/OPTIONS/verb override.\n\nSeverity: Medium",
