  "Test if API handles encryption and decryption failures without leaking key information": "Steps:\n\n1. Send inputs designed to break the endpoint: bad types, malformed JSON/XML, SQL metacharacters ('), oversized payloads, and unexpected routes.\n2. Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it. Read the full error response.\n3. Look specifically for internal implementation details in the body, headers, or status.\n4. Force a 500 (type confusion, division, null) to surface unhandled-exception output.\n5. Collect every internal detail leaked to build a picture of the backend.\n6. Recommend generic errors + server-side logging of the detail instead.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nAPI error responses disclose internal implementation details, giving an attacker internal information useful for further attacks.\n\nSeverity: Medium",
