  "Test if API versioning mechanism prevents access to deprecated versions": "Steps:\n\n1. Enumerate API versions (path /v1/,/v2/,/v3/ and version headers/Accept) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Take a secured action on the current version, then replay it on the older/deprecated version.\n3. Compare: does the old version skip auth, rate limits, or authorization the new one enforces?\n4. Test object access and privileged actions specifically on the legacy version.\n5. Confirm any security control that’s weaker/missing on an older version.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nDeprecated/older API versions remain reachable with weaker (or missing) security controls than the current version, so attackers use the legacy version to bypass fixes.\n\nSeverity: High",
  "Check if older API versions maintain the same security controls as current version": "Steps:\n\n1. Enumerate API versions (path /v1/,/v2/,/v3/ and version headers/Accept) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Take a secured action on the current version, then replay it on the older/deprecated version.\n3. Compare: does the old version skip auth, rate limits, or authorization the new one enforces?\n4. Test object access and privileged actions specifically on the legacy version.\n5. Confirm any security control that’s weaker/missing on an older version.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nDeprecated/older API versions remain reachable with weaker (or missing) security controls than the current version, so attackers use the legacy version to bypass fixes.\n\nSeverity: High",
  "Test if API version in URL path can be manipulated to access other versions": "Steps:\n\n1. Identify how the version is selected (URL path, Accept header, custom X-API-Version) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Tamper the version selector: change the path segment, inject/override the version header, or send conflicting values.\n3. See if you can force an internal/hidden/older version or cause inconsistent routing.\n4. Test whether version manipulation bypasses version-specific security (auth/validation).\n5. Confirm version-selector manipulation changes enforcement.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API version selector (path/header) can be manipulated to reach hidden/older versions or bypass version-specific security controls.\n\nSeverity: Medium–High",
  "Verify if API version header can be injected to bypass version-specific security": "Steps:\n\n1. Identify how the version is selected (URL path, Accept header, custom X-API-Version) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Tamper the version selector: change the path segment, inject/override the version header, or send conflicting values.\n3. See if you can force an internal/hidden/older version or cause inconsistent routing.\n4. Test whether version manipulation bypasses version-specific security (auth/validation).\n5. Confirm version-selector manipulation changes enforcement.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API version selector (path/header) can be manipulated to reach hidden/older versions or bypass version-specific security controls.\n\nSeverity: Medium–High",
