  "Test if API documentation GraphQL playground is accessible in production": "Steps:\n\n1. Probe common API-docs paths:\nfor p in swagger-ui swagger.json openapi.json api-docs v2/api-docs redoc graphql docs; do curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code} /$p\\n\" https://target.com/$p; done\n2. Open any that return 200 without authentication.\n3. Public API docs expose the full endpoint/parameter map to anyone.\n4. Import the spec (OpenAPI/Swagger) into Burp/Postman for testing.\n5. Report internet-exposed documentation that reveals internal/admin operations.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nAPI documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI/GraphQL) is accessible without authentication, handing an attacker the complete endpoint and schema map.\n\nSeverity: Low–Medium",
