  "Check if API webhook endpoint performs TLS certificate validation": "Steps:\n\n1. Review the webhook feature and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Test the controllable webhook URL for SSRF (internal/metadata addresses) — Use a Burp Collaborator / interactsh URL as the payload target and watch for a callback (DNS/HTTP) that proves the request left the server.\n3. Check payload signing/verification and registration authorization.\n4. Test retry limits and delivery to unintended targets.\n5. Confirm and document the specific weakness described in this check.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe webhook mechanism does not securely validate URLs, authenticate delivery, sign payloads, or bound retries, exposing SSRF/forgery/abuse.\n\nSeverity: High",
