  "Test for API versioning security between v1 and v2 endpoints": "Steps:\n\n1. Enumerate API versions (path /v1/,/v2/,/v3/ and version headers/Accept) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Take a secured action on the current version, then replay it on the older/deprecated version.\n3. Compare: does the old version skip auth, rate limits, or authorization the new one enforces?\n4. Test object access and privileged actions specifically on the legacy version.\n5. Confirm any security control that’s weaker/missing on an older version.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nDeprecated/older API versions remain reachable with weaker (or missing) security controls than the current version, so attackers use the legacy version to bypass fixes.\n\nSeverity: High",
  "Test for API authentication bypass on deprecated endpoints": "Steps:\n\n1. Enumerate API versions (path /v1/,/v2/,/v3/ and version headers/Accept) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Take a secured action on the current version, then replay it on the older/deprecated version.\n3. Compare: does the old version skip auth, rate limits, or authorization the new one enforces?\n4. Test object access and privileged actions specifically on the legacy version.\n5. Confirm any security control that’s weaker/missing on an older version.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nDeprecated/older API versions remain reachable with weaker (or missing) security controls than the current version, so attackers use the legacy version to bypass fixes.\n\nSeverity: High",
  "Test for API rate limiting on deprecated version endpoints": "Steps:\n\n1. Enumerate API versions (path /v1/,/v2/,/v3/ and version headers/Accept) and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Take a secured action on the current version, then replay it on the older/deprecated version.\n3. Compare: does the old version skip auth, rate limits, or authorization the new one enforces?\n4. Test object access and privileged actions specifically on the legacy version.\n5. Confirm any security control that’s weaker/missing on an older version.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nDeprecated/older API versions remain reachable with weaker (or missing) security controls than the current version, so attackers use the legacy version to bypass fixes.\n\nSeverity: High",
