  "Test for mass assignment via category_id in classification API": "Steps:\n\n1. Find a create/update API request and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Enumerate extra parameters the API might bind: role, isAdmin, permission, group, verified, status, price, owner, id.\n3. Add these fields to the JSON body one by one with privileged values and resend.\n4. Check via a follow-up read whether any injected field was persisted.\n5. Try nested objects, alternate casing, and duplicate keys to bypass naive filters.\n6. Confirm impact (privilege escalation, price/ownership tampering) with the modified object.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API auto-binds request-body fields to the object without an allow-list, letting an attacker set sensitive attributes (mass assignment / over-posting).\n\nSeverity: High",
