  "Test for API data filtering bypass via parameter injection": "Steps:\n\n1. Call a normal read endpoint and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Inspect the raw JSON response (not just what the UI shows) for extra fields: password hashes, tokens, internal ids, PII, flags.\n3. APIs often return the full object and rely on the client to hide fields.\n4. Check list/search endpoints too — they may leak other users’ data in bulk.\n5. Confirm and document sensitive fields exposed beyond what’s needed.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API returns more data than the client needs (internal fields, PII, secrets), relying on client-side filtering — excessive data exposure.\n\nSeverity: Medium–High",
