  "Test for SQL injection in API query parameters": "Steps:\n\n1. Identify the API endpoint and Capture the request in Burp Suite (Proxy → HTTP history) and send it to Repeater so you can tamper and replay it.\n2. Target each query-string parameter (?q=PAYLOAD).\n3. Send SQL injection payloads (authorized only):\n' OR '1'='1\n1' AND SLEEP(5)-- -\n1 UNION SELECT NULL,version()-- -\n4. Confirm with a time-based payload so you don’t rely on visible errors:\n1' AND SLEEP(5)-- -\n5. Watch for time delays (blind), SQL/parse errors, or authentication/logic changes.\n6. Confirm and document impact (data extraction, command output, callback, or auth/logic bypass).\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nUser input in query-string parameter (?q=PAYLOAD) reaches a backend interpreter/query without sanitisation, allowing SQL injection.\n\nSeverity: Critical",
