  "Test for webhook signature algorithm manipulation": "Steps:\n\n1. Register a webhook and capture a delivered payload to your endpoint.\n2. Check whether it includes a signature header (X-Signature / X-Hub-Signature) and how it’s computed.\n3. Replay the payload with modified content and the same/absent signature to your receiver.\n4. If your receiver (or the API’s verification) accepts a tampered/unsigned payload, integrity isn’t enforced.\n5. Also test signature bypasses: empty signature, wrong algorithm, and timing/replay of old signed payloads.\n6. Confirm forged webhook events are accepted as genuine.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nWebhook payloads aren’t signed (or signatures aren’t verified), so an attacker can forge or tamper with webhook events.\n\nSeverity: Medium",
