  "Test API token security: JWT token algorithm confusion attack (RS256 to HS256)": "Steps:\n\n1. Grab a JWT and decode its header/payload.\n2. Test alg:none (strip signature) and algorithm confusion (RS256→HS256 signing with the public key).\n3. Tamper claims (sub, role, exp) and see if the server accepts the modified token.\n4. Test a weak HMAC secret with jwt_tool / hashcat, and kid injection/path traversal.\n5. Confirm any accepted forged/tampered token.\n\nVulnerable When:\n\nThe API accepts JWTs with weak/misconfigured signature validation (alg:none, algorithm confusion, weak secret, kid abuse), allowing token forgery.\n\nSeverity: High–Critical",
